{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeJGYxn2wzMDs9fix2h7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've set up the project in `/work`. It uses **`fsevents`** (v2.3.3, the standard package wrapping the macOS FSEvents API) for native change notifications. I haven't been able to watch any real files yet, because this machine is Linux and FSEvents only exists on macOS.\n\n**What I created:**\n- `package.json`: the project is named `fswatch-macos` and needs Node 18 or later. It has a `fswatch-macos` command and `start`/`test` scripts.\n- `src/index.js`: provides `watch(path, onEvent)`, which reports each change with its path, event type (created, modified, renamed, etc.), and whether it's a file or directory. It returns an async `stop()` function. There's also an `isSupported()` check.\n- `bin/fswatch-macos.js`: a command-line tool, `npx fswatch-macos [path]`. It prints one JSON line per change and shuts down cleanly on Ctrl+C.\n- `.gitignore`, `README.md` and `package-lock.json`.\n\n**One choice to know about:** `fsevents` is an *optional* dependency, and I removed the setting that limited the package to macOS. With that setting, a normal `npm install` failed on this Linux machine. Now `npm install` works on Linux and CI, and `watch()` throws a clear error there instead.\n\n**What I tested:** `npm install` succeeds and `fsevents` 2.3.3 is in the lockfile. On Linux, `isSupported()` returns `false` and the command-line tool exits with code 1 and a clear message. To check that events actually come through, run `npx fswatch-macos .` on a Mac and change some files.\n\nI haven't committed anything. If you'd rather support Linux and Windows as well later, `@parcel/watcher` is a cross-platform option that still uses FSEvents on macOS."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":18438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"697572ce-6d94-4498-89f9-67148758b22c","uuid":"16d45266-8be2-4491-ba78-25450225ed82","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:44:00.071Z","request_id":"req_011CfeJGYbC8AJRKPU3yQrT7"}
